The invention concerns a uniform solid particulate composition based on urea ammonium sulphate, containing urea ammonium sulphate together with a phosphoric triamide-type urease inhibitor. This urea ammonium sulphate-based composition is additionally defined by at least one of the following features:  
a) it contains, based on the total weight of the composition, no more than 5% by weight of one or more inorganic or organic alkaline or alkaline-generating substances capable of reacting or interacting with ammonium sulphate;  
b) the phosphoric triamide-type urease inhibitor is present as solid particles;  
c) the urea ammonium sulphate particulate material is provided with a coating that prevents caking and/or repels moisture.  

The composition of the invention exhibits enhanced effectiveness in limiting ammonia losses caused by urease activity in soil and is especially useful as a fertilizer.  

The invention also covers a process for producing a uniform, solid, particulate urea ammonium sulphate-based composition that includes urea, ammonium sulphate, and a phosphoric triamide-type urease inhibitor, particularly N-(n-butyl) thiophosphoric triamide (nBTPT). In addition, the invention relates to a kit-of-parts composition comprising:  
a) one or more alkaline or alkaline-forming inorganic compounds capable of interacting with ammonium sulphate;  
b) a phosphoric triamide-type urease inhibitor in either solid particulate or liquid form, preferably N-(n-butyl) thiophosphoric triamide (nBTPT); and  
c) optionally, one or more substances that provide anticaking and/or moisture-repellent properties.
